 ("p", "Opposite the beach stand two large high-rise complexes: Oceanus and Scenia Bay. Oceanus consists of five huge high-rise buildings, and inside it there is a “Russian” neighbourhood with Russian shops and cafés. The North has a very close-knit and strong Russian community, so there is a lot of contact with fellow countrymen."),
 ("g", ["6383", "6382"]),
 ("p", "In the far North there is large-scale construction going on; I think in three or four years there will be a big new district with hotels, restaurants, parks and beaches."),
 ("p", "The new district is home to the Vietnamese theatre Đó Theatre with the wonderful show Life Puppets. That is where I recommend everyone to go!"),
 ("g", ["6388"]),
 ("h2", "The West of Nha Trang — a district for everyday life"),
 ("p", "The West lies deep inside the city, towards the mountains."),
 ("g", ["6323"]),
 ("p", "There is no beachfront here and no such concentration of tourist hotels as in the Centre. Instead you can see the calm side of Nha Trang: ordinary city life."),
 ("p", "The West is a large, lived-in district full of contrasts."),
 ("p", "Closer to the Centre there are old Vietnamese neighbourhoods with small shops and cafés. Further on begin modern residential complexes and new private houses, which are often rented out to foreigners for the long term. Such houses are usually rented by large families who come to Nha Trang for a long time."),
 ("p", "The West has large shopping centres — a significant difference from some other residential districts. Here you will find GO! Nha Trang, a big hypermarket and shopping complex, and Lotte Mart, a supermarket on 23 Tháng 10 street."),
 ("p", "The West of Nha Trang is for ordinary, calm, everyday life. Here Nha Trang stops being a resort and becomes a city where people simply live."),
